From 1e8d405a37d4c2f384ea7c2c31d99112ff680780 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude Lane A <lane-a@local.invalid>
Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 18:47:30 +0530
Subject: [PATCH 18/18] feat(tools): caption only the streamer, not game
 dialogue (--streamer-words-only)

On a stream the game and the mic share one audio track, so transcripts of a
GTA VI cutscene caption the game characters (Luffy: "CAPTION ONLY SHOULD SAY
BY STREAMER"). Games subtitle their own dialogue (white text, dark outline,
bottom centre): per second, the share of bright colourless pixels touching
dark ones in that zone marks a game subtitle (measured on Clix windows:
2.4-13.7 with a subtitle, exactly 0.0 without; threshold 1.5). Words spoken
during those seconds are dropped from the transcript cache the caption
builder reads (original kept as .transcript_cache.full.json).
Tried and rejected first: a facecam mouth-movement rule (kept game lines:
the streamer's face moves while watching) and OpenCode's burned_captions
band detector (0/37 s found: tuned for large caption bands).
Result on a cutscene window: subtitles in 28/37 s, 11 of 101 words kept.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 tools/phase2/auto_edit.py | 79 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 79 insertions(+)

